# ── Local-dev environment variables ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env and uncomment / adjust as needed.
# .env is gitignored; .env.sample is committed and kept up to date.
#
# All variables MUST be prefixed VITE_ to be exposed to the browser bundle
# at build time (Vite replaces import.meta.env.VITE_* at bundle time).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# VITE_USE_MOCK
#   Set to "true" to run the SPA entirely on mock data with NO backend.
#   The app skips every fetch() call and returns data from
#   src/mocks/cases.ts directly.  Useful for:
#     • rapid front-end dev when the Function App is not running
#     • demos / offline presentations
#     • CI/CD lint + build checks that must not hit Azure
#
#   When omitted (or set to anything other than "true"), the app calls the
#   real /api/* endpoints.
#
#   Note: when running `npm run dev` (Vite dev server, import.meta.env.DEV=true)
#   the app ALSO falls back to mock data automatically on any fetch error —
#   you only need this var to skip the fetch entirely from the first call.
#   In production builds (npm run build / Azure SWA deployment) a failed fetch
#   throws and shows an error state — the silent mock fallback is disabled.
#
VITE_USE_MOCK=true
